---
import EvidenceFrame from '../../components/EvidenceFrame.astro';
import FeatureBlock from '../../components/FeatureBlock.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;

const surfaces = [
  {
    index: '01',
    eyebrow: 'Observatory',
    title: 'A legible state before data arrives',
    description: 'The landing surface gives an incomplete day a useful shape: current phase, recovery state, energy field, and a suggested next action remain readable before every signal is available.',
    items: ['Current phase and timing', 'Recovery and signal status', 'Suggested next action'],
  },
  {
    index: '02',
    eyebrow: 'Instruments',
    title: 'Signals organized by physiological role',
    description: 'The Instrument Room groups sleep, recovery, activity, respiration, and cognition so each signal can be read by physiological role rather than as an undifferentiated dashboard.',
    items: ['Sleep architecture', 'HRV and resting heart rate', 'Movement load and breath rhythm'],
  },
  {
    index: '03',
    eyebrow: 'Atlas',
    title: 'Daily observations become recurring traces',
    description: 'The Pattern Atlas is the longitudinal view: a place for daily metrics to accumulate into recognizable rhythms, changes, and recurring conditions over time.',
    items: ['Recurring trace surface', 'Daily observation history', 'Longitudinal pattern view'],
  },
  {
    index: '04',
    eyebrow: 'System',
    title: 'Local data stays understandable and portable',
    description: 'The System route brings browser storage, import/export, historical memory, manual entry, and Android Health Connect settings into one maintenance surface.',
    items: ['Local JSON import/export', 'Historical archive kept separate from scoring', 'Browser and Android behavior distinguished'],
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Energy Engine case study — Chad Hamilton"
  description="A case study of Energy Engine, a personal physiology observatory for energy, recovery, rhythm, and change over time."
>
  <article class="case-study">
    <header class="case-hero section-pad">
      <div class="shell">
        <a class="back-link" href={`${base}#work`}><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Selected work</a>
        <div class="case-hero__grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Case study / Energy Engine</p>
            <h1>A physiology observatory for reading rhythm, recovery, and change.</h1>
          </div>
          <div class="case-hero__summary">
            <p>Energy Engine organizes a changing physiological picture into four connected rooms: the present state, contributing signals, recurring patterns, and the data controls behind them.</p>
            <div class="tag-row">
              <span>Physiology interface</span>
              <span>Local-first data</span>
              <span>Responsive web app</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="case-visual shell">
      <EvidenceFrame
        src={`${base}images/projects/energy/desktop-landing.png`}
        alt="Energy Engine Observatory showing an untracked phase, no recovery signal, and an energy field awaiting telemetry"
        label="Physiology Observatory / Desktop"
        caption="The Observatory keeps phase, recovery, energy, and the next useful action visible even before a day has enough signals to interpret."
        width={1440}
        height={1000}
        eager={true}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="case-facts section-pad-sm">
      <div class="shell case-facts__grid">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Role</span><strong>Design, prototyping, systems documentation</strong></div>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Experience</span><strong>Responsive observatory with four connected surfaces</strong></div>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Inputs</span><strong>Manual observations and Android-connected signals</strong></div>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Data model</span><strong>Present state, instruments, patterns, and local controls</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad section-rule">
      <div class="shell narrative-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Context / 01</p>
          <h2>Make a changing state useful before it becomes complete.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Energy is rarely one signal. Sleep, time awake, recovery, movement, breath, and daily context can point in different directions, and their meaning changes as the day unfolds.</p>
          <p>The observatory metaphor gives those layers separate responsibilities. The opening view answers “where am I now?”, Instruments shows what contributes to that state, Atlas looks for repetition over time, and System keeps the underlying data manageable.</p>
          <p class="callout"><strong>Design principle:</strong> when information is missing, the interface stays useful through clear status, manual input, and a concrete next action rather than forcing a definitive score.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad section-dark">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-heading section-heading--light section-heading--split">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">System surfaces / 02</p>
            <h2>Four rooms, each with a distinct responsibility.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The system’s information architecture keeps immediate interpretation, signal inspection, longitudinal patterns, and maintenance controls separate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid feature-grid--case">
          {surfaces.map((surface) => <FeatureBlock {...surface} />)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad section-rule">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Responsive experience / 03</p>
            <h2>Desktop structure, mobile continuity.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Desktop creates room for comparison across instruments. Mobile preserves the same navigation and state language while turning each room into a focused vertical reading.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="evidence-pair">
          <EvidenceFrame
            src={`${base}images/projects/energy/desktop-instruments.png`}
            alt="Desktop Energy Engine Instrument Room in a manual and unlinked browser state"
            label="Instruments / Desktop"
            caption="Signal categories are organized by role, with manual and connected states visible where decisions are made."
            width={1440}
            height={1196}
          />
          <EvidenceFrame
            src={`${base}images/projects/energy/mobile-instruments.png`}
            alt="Mobile Energy Engine Instrument Room with sleep, recovery, activity, respiration, and cognition controls"
            label="Instruments / Mobile"
            caption="The same instrument model becomes a clear vertical sequence on mobile."
            width={390}
            height={904}
            tone="light"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="evidence-pair evidence-pair--reverse">
          <EvidenceFrame
            src={`${base}images/projects/energy/mobile-atlas.png`}
            alt="Mobile Pattern Atlas empty state asking for daily metrics"
            label="Atlas / Mobile"
            caption="The mobile Atlas explains what daily observations will become before a recurring trace is available."
            width={390}
            height={844}
            tone="light"
          />
          <EvidenceFrame
            src={`${base}images/projects/energy/desktop-atlas.png`}
            alt="Desktop Pattern Atlas empty state with no observations"
            label="Atlas / Desktop"
            caption="The desktop Atlas holds space for recurring traces while keeping the next step easy to understand."
            width={1440}
            height={1000}
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad system-section">
      <div class="shell system-section__grid">
        <div class="system-section__copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Data and platform / 04</p>
          <h2>Manual observations and connected signals share one model.</h2>
          <p>The System surface keeps local browser data usable on its own while describing the Android path for automatic signals through Samsung Health and Health Connect.</p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Manual entries take precedence over automatic values.</li>
            <li>Historical archive observations are stored apart from live scoring.</li>
            <li>Extended context is labeled as not used in scoring.</li>
            <li>The interface states that nothing is written back through Health Connect.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="fine-print">The browser experience remains useful through manual entry; the Android host extends the same system with connected health signals.</p>
        </div>
        <EvidenceFrame
          src={`${base}images/projects/energy/mobile-system.png`}
          alt="Long mobile System Controls page showing local data, historical memory, and Health Connect sections"
          label="System controls / Mobile"
          caption="Full-page capture of the empty browser state. The interface reports zero days on file and no archive imported."
          width={390}
          height={5146}
          tone="light"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad section-rule">
      <div class="shell outcome-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Product qualities / 05</p>
          <h2>A calm interface for incomplete, personal data.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="outcome-grid__lists">
          <div>
            <h3>What the design prioritizes</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Separate views for state, signals, patterns, and maintenance</li>
              <li>Useful guidance when data is incomplete</li>
              <li>Manual observations beside connected-signal states</li>
              <li>Local import, export, and reset controls</li>
              <li>Responsive continuity from desktop to mobile</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Responsible product boundaries</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>A personal observation tool, not a medical diagnosis</li>
              <li>Interpretations stay connected to their contributing signals</li>
              <li>Manual values take precedence when intentionally entered</li>
              <li>Historical context remains separate from live scoring</li>
              <li>Connected health data is read, not written back</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav class="case-next" aria-label="Project navigation">
      <div class="shell case-next__inner">
        <span>Next project</span>
        <a href={`${base}projects/semantic-archaeology/`}>Semantic Archaeology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </article>
</Layout>